IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ia-types`

-- Insurance Act 2015 (UK) — GOALS 1 AND 2: APPLICATION; THE DUTY OF FAIR
-- PRESENTATION AND THE INSURER'S REMEDIES (ss 1, 2, 3, 7, 8, 22; Sch 1
-- Part 1).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2015-4.txt.

§ `Goal 1 — application`

-- s 22(3) "“the relevant period” means the period of 18 months beginning with
-- the day on which this Act is passed" (12 February 2015). It ends on the day
-- before the corresponding date 18 months later: 11 August 2016.
@ref s 22(3)
`the last day of the relevant period` MEANS
    Date (Day (`add months` (Date 12 2 2015) 18) MINUS 1)

-- s 2(1) "This Part applies to non-consumer insurance contracts only."
-- s 22(1)-(2): Parts 2, 3 and 4 apply only to contracts entered into after
-- the end of the relevant period.
@ref ss 1, 2(1), 22(1)-(3)
@export Whether Parts 2 to 4 of the Insurance Act 2015 (UK) (fair presentation, warranties and terms, fraudulent claims) apply to a contract: a non-consumer insurance contract entered into after the end of the relevant period of 18 months beginning with 12 February 2015, that is on or after 12 August 2016. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN k IS A `Contract facts`  @desc Whether the contract is a consumer insurance contract, and the day it was entered into
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Parts 2 to 4 apply to` k IF
        NOT (k's `a consumer insurance contract`)
    AND k's `entered into on` GREATER THAN `the last day of the relevant period`

-- s 22(2) "Parts 3 and 4 of this Act apply only in relation to contracts of
-- insurance entered into after the end of the relevant period". Unlike
-- Part 2 (s 2(1)), they are not limited to non-consumer contracts (added
-- after the independent pass).
@ref s 22(2)-(3)
@export Whether Parts 3 and 4 of the Insurance Act 2015 (UK) (warranties and other terms, fraudulent claims) apply to a contract of insurance, consumer or not: entered into after the end of the relevant period, that is on or after 12 August 2016. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN k IS A `Contract facts`  @desc The day the contract was entered into
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Parts 3 and 4 apply to` k IF
    k's `entered into on` GREATER THAN `the last day of the relevant period`

§ `Goal 2 — the duty of fair presentation`

-- s 3(4) "The disclosure required is as follows, except as provided in
-- subsection (5)— (a) disclosure of every material circumstance which the
-- insured knows or ought to know, or (b) failing that, disclosure which gives
-- the insurer sufficient information to put a prudent insurer on notice that
-- it needs to make further enquiries". (5) "In the absence of enquiry,
-- subsection (4) does not require the insured to disclose a circumstance if—
-- (a) it diminishes the risk, (b) the insurer knows it, (c) the insurer ought
-- to know it, (d) the insurer is presumed to know it, or (e) it is something
-- as to which the insurer waives information."
@ref s 3(4)-(5)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure required by s 3(4) was made of` c IF
        NOT (c's `material`)
    OR  NOT (c's `the insured knows or ought to know it`)
    OR  c's `disclosed`
    OR  c's `enough disclosed to put a prudent insurer on notice`
    OR  (    NOT (c's `the insurer enquired about it`)
         AND (   c's `it diminishes the risk`
              OR c's `the insurer knows it`
              OR c's `the insurer ought to know it`
              OR c's `the insurer is presumed to know it`
              OR c's `the insurer waives information about it`))

-- s 3(3) "A fair presentation of the risk is one— (a) which makes the
-- disclosure required by subsection (4), (b) which makes that disclosure in a
-- manner which would be reasonably clear and accessible to a prudent insurer,
-- and (c) in which every material representation as to a matter of fact is
-- substantially correct, and every material representation as to a matter of
-- expectation or belief is made in good faith."
@ref s 3(1), (3)
@export Whether the insured made a fair presentation of the risk under s 3 of the Insurance Act 2015 (UK): every material circumstance it knows or ought to know disclosed (or enough to put a prudent insurer on notice), unless, absent enquiry, s 3(5) excuses it; reasonably clear and accessible; material representations of fact substantially correct and of expectation or belief in good faith. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Presentation`  @desc Each circumstance, how the presentation was made, and the representations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a fair presentation was made in` p IF
        all (GIVEN c YIELD `the disclosure required by s 3(4) was made of` c) (p's `circumstances`)
    AND p's `reasonably clear and accessible to a prudent insurer`
    AND p's `material representations of fact substantially correct`
    AND p's `material representations of expectation or belief in good faith`

-- s 8(1) "The insurer has a remedy ... only if the insurer shows that, but
-- for the breach, the insurer— (a) would not have entered into the contract
-- of insurance at all, or (b) would have done so only on different terms." A
-- higher premium is a different term.
@ref s 8(1), (3)
@export Whether there is a qualifying breach of the duty of fair presentation under s 8 of the Insurance Act 2015 (UK): no fair presentation, and but for the breach the insurer would not have entered into the contract at all, or only on different terms (including a higher premium). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Presentation`                       @desc The presentation
      w IS A `What the insurer would have done`   @desc What the insurer would have done but for the breach
      x IS A `Money facts`                        @desc The premium actually charged
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a qualifying breach in` p `given` w `and` x IF
        NOT (`a fair presentation was made in` p)
    AND inducement
    WHERE
        inducement MEANS
            CONSIDER w
            WHEN `the same contract on the same terms` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `no contract on any terms` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the contract, on these terms` different higher THEN
                different OR higher GREATER THAN x's `the premium actually charged`

§§ `The insurer's remedies (Sch 1 Part 1)`

DECLARE `Remedy` HAS
    `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `must return the premiums paid`                     IS A NUMBER
    `contract treated as on the different terms`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount payable on the claim`                       IS A NUMBER

-- Sch 1 para 2 "If a qualifying breach was deliberate or reckless, the
-- insurer— (a) may avoid the contract and refuse all claims, and (b) need not
-- return any of the premiums paid." Para 4: not on any terms — avoid, refuse
-- all claims, return the premiums. Para 5: different terms "if the insurer so
-- requires". Para 6: a higher premium — "the insurer need pay on the claim
-- only X% of what it would otherwise have been under an obligation to pay
-- under the terms of the contract (or, if applicable, under the different
-- terms ...)", X = (premium actually charged ÷ higher premium) × 100. Each
-- answer is the most the insurer may do. s 8(5): deliberate or reckless if
-- the insured knew it was in breach or did not care.
@ref s 8(4)-(6), Sch 1 paras 2-6
@export What the insurer may do under Schedule 1 Part 1 to the Insurance Act 2015 (UK) for a breach of the duty of fair presentation: with no qualifying breach, nothing (the claim is paid under the contract); deliberate or reckless, avoid and refuse all claims, keeping the premiums; otherwise, avoid and return the premiums if it would not have contracted at all, or apply the different terms and pay only the premium charged ÷ the higher premium of the claim. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Presentation`                       @desc The presentation, and whether the insured knew of the breach or did not care
      w IS A `What the insurer would have done`   @desc What the insurer would have done but for the breach
      x IS A `Money facts`                        @desc Premiums charged and paid, the claim under the actual and the different terms
GIVETH A `Remedy`
`the remedy for the presentation in` p `given` w `and` x MEANS
    IF   NOT (`there is a qualifying breach in` p `given` w `and` x)
    THEN `Remedy` OF FALSE, 0, FALSE, x's `the claim under the actual terms`
    ELSE IF   p's `the insured knew of the breach or did not care`
         THEN `Remedy` OF TRUE, 0, FALSE, 0
         ELSE CONSIDER w
              WHEN `no contract on any terms` THEN `Remedy` OF TRUE, x's `the premiums paid`, FALSE, 0
              WHEN `the contract, on these terms` different higher THEN
                  `Remedy` OF FALSE, 0, requires different, payable different higher
              OTHERWISE `Remedy` OF FALSE, 0, FALSE, x's `the claim under the actual terms`
    WHERE
        GIVEN different IS A BOOLEAN
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        -- Para 5 applies "if the insurer so requires": it is taken to require
        -- the different terms only when they lower the claim (changed after
        -- the independent pass, line 240).
        requires different MEANS
            different AND x's `the claim under the different terms` LESS THAN x's `the claim under the actual terms`
        GIVEN different IS A BOOLEAN
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        base different MEANS
            IF requires different THEN x's `the claim under the different terms` ELSE x's `the claim under the actual terms`
        GIVEN different IS A BOOLEAN, higher IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        payable different higher MEANS
            IF   higher GREATER THAN x's `the premium actually charged`
            THEN base different TIMES (x's `the premium actually charged` DIVIDED BY higher)
            ELSE base different
